  The reel_script says the 3 companies were fined for 'சுகாதாரமற்று இருந்த' (being unhygienic), which is consistent, but the reel_script and slides_spec do not mention the inspection being conducted in 'Ashokapuram' as a fact of the article only for industrial establishments; the slides_spec and caption say 'அசோகபுரம் பகுதியில் உள்ள தொழில் நிறுவனங்கள்' correctly, however the slides_spec 'loc' field and 'எங்கே, எப்போது?' slide say the inspection was done 'சுகாதார ஆய்வாளர்கள் ஆய்வு செய்தனர்' without noting the companies were in Ashokapuram only in the reel; minor wording inconsistency.
  The reel_script states 'அபராதம் விதிக்கப்பட்டுள்ளது' before explaining the inspection, and the caption says 'மாநகராட்சி நிர்வாகம், அசோகபுரம் பகுதியில் ... ஆய்வு நடத்தியது' while the article attributes the inspection to health inspectors under the Corporation; this is consistent but the caption's 'Erode 3 firms fined ... | Erode news' English line is an extra English line not in the article's Tamil text (acceptable as a translation of the headline).
  The reel_script omits the article's point that residents are being warned and that awareness materials/handbooks and pamphlets are being distributed door to door; this is an important part of the article's content not reflected in the reel_script.
